  "_comment": "Component recipes, not stat sheets. Each recipe declares exactly three things: FORM (size/volume + positioning offsets), a COMPOSITION of distinct materials (fractions sum to 1.0), and the INTERNAL COMPONENTS (organs) that are pre-installed. It declares NO stat values: existence, the six channel resistances, mass, and sharpness derive from matter; volume from form; strength/move/fine_controls/think_level from the organs a recipe installs. A recipe with matter but no organs is inert. Material and IC references point at data/materials.json and data/internalComponents.json. An internalComponents entry is either an organ type string (type-default grants) or an object { type, grants? } whose grants override the organ type's defaults for that recipe's instances — e.g. droidRollingBall's strengthCore override (120) lets the 12-volume iron wheels bear the heaviest equipable item (T1 needs 1.5 x 78 = 117 strength) where the 10-volume centralBall cannot spare room for a second heavy item.",
